{"event": "text", "text": "In Vulkan, **timeline semaphores** are a synchronization primitive that allows CPU-side and GPU-side waits and signals to be **monotonically increasing 64-bit values**. Unlike binary semaphores (which are single-use and reset automatically), timeline semaphores maintain a persistent counter and can be waited on", "host_s": 37.8248}
